<tool id="neutrons_radar_pd_interactive_prototype" tool_type="interactive" name="RADAR-PD Interactive" version="0.3.60" profile="22.01">
    <description>configure, run, monitor, recover, and inspect Full or Rapid RADAR-PD analyses</description>
    <creator>
        <person name="Lalit Yadav"/>
        <organization url="https://www.ornl.gov/" name="ORNL"/>
    </creator>
    <requirements>
        <container type="docker" shell="/bin/bash">savannah.ornl.gov/radar-pd/radar-pd-nova:nova-0.3.60</container>
    </requirements>
    <entry_points>
        <entry_point name="RADAR-PD Interactive" label="app_entry" requires_domain="False" requires_path_in_url="True">
            <port>8081</port>
        </entry_point>
    </entry_points>
    <environment_variables>
        <environment_variable name="GALAXY_URL">$__galaxy_url__</environment_variable>
        <environment_variable name="GALAXY_API_KEY" inject="api_key"/>
        <environment_variable name="HISTORY_ID">$__history_id__</environment_variable>
        <environment_variable name="EP_PATH" inject="entry_point_path_for_label">app_entry</environment_variable>
        <environment_variable name="RADAR_PD_SNS_ROOT">/SNS</environment_variable>
        <environment_variable name="RADAR_PD_HFIR_ROOT">/HFIR</environment_variable>
    </environment_variables>
    <command><![CDATA[
        supervisord -c /etc/supervisord.conf > >(tee -a $output) 2> >(tee -a $output >&2)
    ]]></command>
    <inputs/>
    <outputs>
        <data format="txt" name="output" label="RADAR-PD Interactive console output"/>
    </outputs>
    <help><![CDATA[
RADAR-PD Interactive provides one shared setup experience for Full RADAR-PD and Rapid Hypothesis Mode. It can upload local files, reuse datasets in the current Galaxy history, resolve SNS IPTS inputs, submit the existing batch Analyze tool, show progress, recover earlier runs, render interactive results, and expose reproducible artifacts.

The scientific calculation runs as a normal Galaxy job. Closing this interactive session does not cancel that job or remove its history outputs.
    ]]></help>
</tool>
